FLOORFORGE_40 — the live console's copy describes a one-machine run; it runs two.

WHAT IS WRONG

FLOORFORGE_30 turned /live into a two-machine job. The ForgeSand D1 works the
open field, parks, and the ForgeEdge E1 cuts the 12 cm band at the wall a drum
physically cannot reach; they alternate once per grit under separate device ids
(FF-S001, FF-E001), and the finished run writes field coverage and perimeter
coverage into the completion report as two separately attributed figures.

The stage, the HUD and the status chip were all updated to follow whichever
machine is actually cutting. Three surfaces were not:

  app/live/page.tsx        h1 "Watch a D1 run the floor.", the intro, and the
                           <meta name="description"> all announced one machine.
  components/LiveJobConsole.tsx
                           the honesty note read "A ForgeSand D1 does not exist
                           yet" — denying the existence of one machine on a page
                           that simulates two.
  app/page.tsx             the homepage card linking to /live described a single
                           D1 and a bullet reading "Simulated machine".

So the page understated what it does, and it contradicted public/llms.txt, which
has described the two-machine run since FLOORFORGE_37. On a site whose entire
credibility rests on its own description being accurate, a page describing itself
wrongly is a defect of the same class as a wrong number.

WHAT THIS CHANGES

Copy only. No behaviour, no styling, no layout, no new claim.

  * The headline names the machine count and what the console proves:
    "Two machines. One floor. Every event accounted for."
  * The intro describes the actual sequence — field, park, perimeter, alternate
    once per grit — and the split figures the report receives.
  * Machine names and the edge gap are READ FROM lib/robots.ts (getRobot("sand"),
    getRobot("edge"), edgeGapM * 100) rather than typed, so this cannot drift
    again silently. "12 cm" on the page is 0.12 m from the spec.

THE DISCLAIMERS GOT STRONGER, NOT WEAKER

Per the standing constraint, nothing was removed, shortened, softened or moved:

  before: "A ForgeSand D1 does not exist yet."
  after:  "Neither a ForgeSand D1 nor a ForgeEdge E1 exists yet."

  before: "No FloorForge machine has refinished a floor, and none is connected
           here."
  after:  unchanged, plus "Neither the D1 nor the E1 has been built."

  eyebrow: "SIMULATED MACHINE" -> "SIMULATED MACHINES"
  card bullet: "Simulated machine, real data path" -> "Simulated machines, ..."

No performance figure, customer count, testimonial, case study, certification or
partner logo was added. Nothing implies a shipped product or an existing
customer.

