NOT FIXED HERE, REPORTED HONESTLY

audit/scripts/contrast.mjs exits 1 with 45 rendered-contrast failures. NONE are
on /live and none are on text this patch touches. Roughly two thirds are false
positives — sr-only text, which the script measures as white-on-white because it
is clipped to 1px. The remainder look real: overlay labels on the concept-render
carousel at 4.44:1, /systems at 3.56:1, /simulator's orbit hint at 4.23:1 and
/pro-simulator at 4.43:1, all against the 4.5:1 requirement. axe does not catch
these because it declines to judge text over an image. That is the next patch,
not this one.

